* fix(rundir): pin golden fixture 01 resolving through the run directory (#98)

* feat(ops): verified ledger backup before it is called good (#160)

pg_dump alone proves nothing: it can exit 0 on a dump that will not
restore, or one that restores to a chain that no longer matches what
was sealed. scripts/backup-ledger.sh restores every dump into a
throwaway database in the same container, extracts the restored
event_hash column, and adjudicates it against the sealed segments with
the existing runbooks/verify-rebuilt-index.sh gate before the backup
is kept and reported OK -- the check runbooks/index-rebuild.md §0
describes for a restore, run here at backup time instead, per #160's
request that a bad backup be caught the day it is made.

A backup with no sealed segments to check against is kept but reported
UNVERIFIED rather than passed quietly; one that restores but disagrees
with a sealed segment is refused as a MISMATCH naming the position.

scripts/backup-ledger-selftest.sh drives this against a real
postgres:16 container loaded with the fourteen committed golden
fixtures through the real append-only and chain-link triggers (BAK-001
green on a matching chain, BAK-002 red on one event's hash altered
after sealing, BAK-003 unverified with no segments, BAK-004 fails
closed with no container). New test IDs, not added to doc 07.

`make innsegl-backup` runs it against the reference stack. Dumps go to
a local ./backups by default ($INNSEGL_BACKUP_DIR to override); doc 05
§2 names WORM object storage as the eventual home but this does not
ship a cloud upload path.

